  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by BioBricks licensing-provenance annotation agent (Claude). stages/01_download.py downloads the ToxValDB v9.7.0 Release zip from Zenodo record 17088058. The authoritative Zenodo record page states its license is Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) - NOT CC0. IMPORTANT DISCREPANCY the reviewer must resolve: the local .bb/provenance.jsonld and .bb/brick.jsonld assert CC0-1.0 / 'Public Domain', and the identical v9.7.0 data is deposited by EPA on Figshare (article 20394501) under CC0 (verified via Figshare API; see sibling brick toxvaldb). Because this brick's actual download source is the Zenodo deposit marked CC BY 4.0, I conservatively adopt the more restrictive attribution class for this brick. CC BY 4.0 permits commercial use with attribution => licenseClass=attribution, merckCommercialUse=permitted. HUMAN REVIEW: (1) decide whether the CC0 Figshare mirror or the CC BY 4.0 Zenodo deposit is the governing distribution, and align brick.jsonld/provenance.jsonld accordingly; (2) ToxValDB is a U.S. Government work aggregating 51 sources - EPA's own contribution is public domain, but preserve attribution to comply with the Zenodo deposit terms; (3) cite Wall/Sayre/Weitekamp/Smith, Computational Toxicology 2025.",
